  "code": [],
  "full": [
    {
      "description": "Exports the user's Audit log: every entry in sequence, each with the hash that chains it to the one before it, the anchor first when \`audit.retention\` pruned its beginning. The CLI's \`audit export\` writes them as JSONL, one entry per line, which \`audit verify --file\` verifies off the machine.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "audit_export",
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Verifies the user's Audit log: every entry's hash chains it to the one before it, and the head file names the last one. Answers that it is intact, or the first sequence that does not verify, so an edited, deleted, reordered or truncated entry, a truncated tail included, shows.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "audit_verify",
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Deletes the caller's entries from the Response cache of the engine's major: those of a domain and its subdomains, of a Run, of a partition, or every one when no filter is given; given filters narrow each other. A body file leaves with the last entry holding it, and nothing of a deleted entry stays in the cache's files. A cache never written is not created; one of a format version the engine cannot read is refused with \`format_version_unsupported\`.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "cache_clear",
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    {
      "description": "Counts the caller's entries in the Response cache of the engine's major, the bodies they hold and the bytes those weigh, by partition, and the bytes the whole cache holds against \`cache.max_size\`. A cache never written counts nothing and is not created; one of a format version the engine cannot read is refused with \`format_version_unsupported\`.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "cache_stats",
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Reads every body file the caller's entries in the Response cache of the engine's major hold, and lists each entry whose file is missing or whose bytes no longer hash to the body stored; it changes nothing, and \`cache.clear\` deletes what it lists. A cache never written holds nothing to verify and is not created; one of a format version the engine cannot read is refused with \`format_version_unsupported\`.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "cache_verify",
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Starts a code-free catalog run, a Run with no handler in the program whose verbs come from the catalog (ADR 0036): an Extraction of a page by a schema, \`extract\`, an Agent task, \`agent\`, or a Plan replayed with no model call, \`plan_replay\`; and answers once it is started. Its Run ID works as \`run.start\`'s. With \`detached\`, the Run outlives the program that started it: closing its value frees only the value, \`run.finish\` waits for its end and \`run.stop\` stops it.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "catalog_run_start",
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": true,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
    },
    {
      "description": "Lists the caller's pins in the known-certificates store: each host whose invalid certificate was accepted on first use, the SHA-256 of its public key, when and by which Run. Another person's pins on a shared Daemon are never listed. A row the engine cannot read is listed without its hash; it stops its host as a changed key.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "certs_list",
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows each setting's effective value, the layer that set it and the layer that locked it, from the built-in defaults, the Operator policy, user configuration, the project configuration given and the run layer: the Connection's own settings with the run values given over them, or a live Run's as it opened when \`run_id\` names one; and lists the keys only the other Product honours as that Product's.",
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "hasObjectSchema": true,
      "id": "config_explain",
      "idempotentHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
    },
    {
      "description": "Says whether the Daemon is live and ready to take a new Run, and why not: what its ops listener's \`/livez\` and \`/readyz\` answer with a status alone.",
